sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphological realism / specimen match: 74/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "The rendered gallery in bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png and docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif produces visually distinct cortical planforms and retinal pullbacks for Klüver's four form-constant families (Tunnel concentric rings, Spiral logarithmic arms, Cobweb radial/circular net, Honeycomb hexagonal lattice) plus the Rhombic lattice, complete with cortical and retinal orientation line segments. However, three of Klüver's four form constants (Tunnel, Spiral, Cobweb) are badged IMPOSED: unstable and Honeycomb is STABLE-coexisting because the model's cubic equations select only the 5th (Rhombic) column, so the classic form constants are produced by hard-coding mode wavevectors in planform_modes rather than emerging from the model (-10 pts). Because lambda_c = 8.68 mm is 3.1x longer than Bressloff et al.'s 2.4-3.2 mm scale (11 cycles vs 30-36 perceived stripes), the retinal pullbacks are roughly 3x coarser than Bressloff et al. (2001) Figs. 31-36 and (2002) Figs. 6-7 (-7 pts). In full-field mode, oblique and hexagonal cortical modes have non-integer azimuthal cycle counts k_y * L / (2*pi) = 11 * sin(theta) across the torus circumference L in addition to foveal narrowing, creating visible phase- discontinuity seams (9.9x on Spiral, 3.4x on Rhombic) and chevron kinks along the left horizontal meridian (-5 pts). Lastly, the contoured gallery panels plot continuous tanh heatmaps with sparse white line segments every 8 cells and the GIF drops contoured mode altogether (contour_mode='noncontoured'), departing from the paper's binary oriented-contour renderings (-4 pts). Evidence: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): 5-column cortical and retinal gallery with orientation line segments, selection badges, and diagnostic panels A-G — bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at d6f3c94, image/png, 1634872 B, 2620×2419 px, artifact_sha256 799d93639f28fa0f81279848de4b8d23b26644a1c8856fdc44c0028d4fc6ba5e (sha256 799d93639f28fa0f81279848de4b8d23b26644a1c8856fdc44c0028d4fc6ba5e), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif (generated output, not in repo): 36-frame 5-preset phase-drift animation rendered in noncontoured mode with uniform_phase=True — docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at d6f3c94, image/gif, 2349709 B, 640×350 px, 36 frames, artifact_sha256 db057a32f49451a8c5ada9698336085308e9d3664d17769f51fa1cf4dda4dae8 (sha256 db057a32f49451a8c5ada9698336085308e9d3664d17769f51fa1cf4dda4dae8), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L982–L1014: planform_modes hard-codes wavevector angles and amplitudes for rings, rays, spiral, cobweb, honeycomb, rhombic, hex_pi, and triangle <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L982-L1014>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1613–L1675: Gallery loop showing 1 selected, 1 stable-coexisting, and 3 imposed-unstable panels with 11 rendered cycles vs 30-36 paper stripes <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1613-L1675>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.74"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Morphological realism / specimen match' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (Cursor agent, blinded second assessor)" .
}

